event: response.output_text.done
data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_069b54ac0ff5886e016aa3e44a7e4c87d293eccdb221d4f59c","logprobs":[],"output_index":1,"sequence_number":6307,"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Transaction Batch Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for individual invocations of CBTRN02C, CBACT04C and CBTRN03C.\n    HTTP paths, JSON envelopes, file bindings and response status mappings are\n    transport conventions, not interfaces implemented by the COBOL sources.\n    An invocation executes one program, not its enclosing JCL schedule.\n    Referenced indexed files must be provisioned by the execution environment.\n    No file-management, backup, merge, fee-processing or scheduling API is implied.\n\n    Input arrays represent sequential files in the supplied order. Indexed-file\n    bindings identify persistent resources; they are not snapshots supplied by\n    the caller. Output arrays expose records written by the program. No\n    transaction-wide atomicity, rollback, retry or idempotency is promised.\n    Earlier writes and OUTPUT opens can have effects even when a run fails.\n\n    Structured records express valid COBOL field representations, not business\n    validation. Character fields are right-padded with spaces to their PIC width.\n    Numeric identifiers retain leading zeros. Decimal strings are converted to\n    signed fixed-point DISPLAY fields. Raw records permit malformed numeric\n    bytes, arbitrary filler and other file-level failure inputs without imposing\n    invented business checks.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    The corpus supplies no HTTP runtime, file resolver, compiler configuration,\n    encoding configuration or implementation of CEE3ABD. Actual execution\n    availability is an environmental precondition, not established by this contract.\n  - |\n    Native DISPLAY sign encoding, character collation and overflow behavior depend\n    on the COBOL runtime. Arithmetic has no ON SIZE ERROR handling. Raw records\n    require the deployment's native record encoding.\n  - |\n    JCL references SORT, IDCAMS, GDGs and REPROC. REPROC in turn references an\n    unsupplied REPROCT control member. None of these utilities or schedules is\n    assumed to execute through these operations.\n  - |\n    TRANFILE is opened OUTPUT by posting, although the JCL describes a transaction\n    master. Existing master contents are not guaranteed to survive or be available\n    for duplicate detection. This contract does not silently change the open to I-O.\npaths:\n  /posting-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Post one sequential daily transaction file\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN02C. Opens DALYTRAN INPUT, TRANFILE OUTPUT,\n        XREFFILE INPUT, DALYREJS OUTPUT, ACCTFILE I-O and TCATBALF I-O,\n        in that order. Empty input is representable.\n\n        Each successfully read record increments the processed counter. Validation\n        first reads the card cross-reference, then the referenced account.\n        Invalid card produces 0100; missing account produces 0101.\n        On an account read, temporary balance is cycleCredit - cycleDebit + amount\n        in S9(9)V99, not currentBalance + amount. A credit limit smaller than this\n        value sets 0102. ExpirationDate less than the first ten characters of\n        originalTimestamp sets 0103 and overrides 0102. Date comparison is\n        alphanumeric, with no calendar validation. Equality passes both checks.\n        Active status, cash limit, merchant, transaction type/category membership,\n        amount positivity and timestamp syntax are not validated.\n\n        Rejections write the original 350-byte record followed by four reason\n        digits and a space-padded 76-character description. Processing continues.\n        Any rejected records cause RETURN-CODE to be set to 4 at normal completion.\n\n        For a valid record, business fields are copied to the output transaction;\n        processingTimestamp is replaced with the current runtime timestamp.\n        Effects occur in this order: create or add amount to the category balance\n        keyed by account/type/category; add amount to account current balance and,\n        for amount >= 0, cycle credit, otherwise add the signed negative amount to\n        cycle debit; write the indexed transaction keyed by transaction ID.\n        A missing category balance with status 23 is created from an initialized\n        record. No duplicate-ID precheck is performed. A duplicate write may fail\n        after balances have changed.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, but the caller\n        neither rechecks that reason nor writes a reject; it still attempts the\n        transaction write. This is not an ordinary 0109 rejection response.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - The bound files support the stated indexed keys and open modes.\n        - Successful posting requires a card mapping and its account; missing mappings remain legal request cases.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions, transactionFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, categoryBalanceFile, rejectFile]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                transactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                rejectFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal program completion, including per-record business rejections.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Calculate category interest and write system transactions\n      description: |\n        Executes CBACT04C. Opens TCATBALF INPUT for sequential indexed-key\n        traversal, XREFFILE INPUT with alternate account key, DISCGRP INPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O and TRANSACT OUTPUT. It does not post or merge its output\n        into the indexed transaction master and does not update category balances.\n\n        For each account encountered, reads the account and the cross-reference\n        by account ID. A nonzero read status is fatal, including a missing record.\n        Rates are looked up by account group, balance transaction type and category.\n        Status 23 triggers a second lookup using the space-padded group DEFAULT\n        and the same type/category. Failure of that fallback is fatal. Other\n        nonzero primary lookup statuses are fatal.\n\n        Each nonzero rate produces one transaction, even for zero or negative\n        category balances or a computed zero amount. Monthly interest equals\n        categoryBalance * annualRate / 1200, assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED,\n        discarding excess fractional digits. Interest is accumulated per account.\n        Zero rates produce no transaction. The fees paragraph does nothing.\n\n        Transaction ID is the ten-character parameter concatenated with a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001, incremented only on generated transactions.\n        The parameter length is not checked and the parameter is not parsed as a\n        date. The JCL example is 2022071800. Generated type is 01, category is\n        numeric 0005, source is System, description begins \"Int. for a/c \" followed\n        by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is monthly interest, merchant ID\n        is zero and merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces. Card number comes from the\n        account-key cross-reference. Original and processing timestamps are both\n        the current runtime timestamp.\n\n        On transition to a different account, the previous account is rewritten:\n        total accumulated interest is added to current balance and both cycle\n        credit and cycle debit are zeroed, including when all its rates were zero.\n        The source's final-account update branch is unreachable in the normal\n        EOF path: EOF is set inside the N branch and the loop then terminates.\n        Consequently the final account is not rewritten at normal EOF, although\n        its generated transactions have already been written. Empty category\n        input generates no transactions and rewrites no accounts.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - TCATBALF supports sequential traversal by account/type/category key.\n        - XREFFILE must support reading its alternate eleven-digit account key.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          INTCALC JCL also binds XREFFIL1 to an alternate-index path, but the\n          program SELECT uses XREFFILE. Availability and selection of that\n          alternate index are not established by the supplied slice.\n        - |\n          More than 999999 generated records exceeds the six-digit suffix\n          capacity; no explicit overflow or collision handling exists.\n        - |\n          TRAN-RECORD is not initialized before generation. Unassigned filler\n          and description suffix bytes depend on working-storage initialization.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [parameterDate, categoryBalanceFile, crossReferenceFile, disclosureGroupFile, accountFile, outputTransactionFile]\n              properties:\n                parameterDate:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: Exact PIC X(10) transaction-ID prefix; arbitrary text is allowed.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n                parameterLength:\n                  type: integer\n                  minimum: -32768\n                  maximum: 32767\n                  description: Linkage S9(4) COMP length. Not inspected by the program; transport supplies 10 when omitted.\n                  default: 10\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                disclosureGroupFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                outputTransactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal completion; generated output is separate from the transaction master.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/InterestResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-report-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN03C against the supplied sequential transaction records.\n        Opens TRANFILE INPUT, TRANREPT OUTPUT, CARDXREF INPUT, TRANTYPE INPUT,\n        TRANCATG INPUT and DATEPARM INPUT. Reads only the first date parameter\n        record: positions 1-10 are start date, position 11 is ignored and positions\n        12-21 are end date; remaining bytes are ignored. Empty DATEPARM sets EOF\n        and produces an empty report. No calendar or start-before-end check exists.\n\n        For each transaction, the first ten characters of processingTimestamp are\n        compared inclusively to the parameter dates. An out-of-range record uses\n        NEXT SENTENCE to skip the remaining loop body. No sorting occurs in this\n        program. Input order is retained; account subtotals actually delimit\n        contiguous card-number groups, not distinct account IDs. Noncontiguous\n        repeats and multiple cards for an account are not consolidated.\n\n        On a card change, the previous group subtotal is written if reporting has\n        started, then card cross-reference is read. Type and composite type/category\n        descriptions are read for every included record. INVALID KEY in any lookup\n        displays the offending key and invokes the abend routine with status 23.\n        These are fatal failures, not skipped records or posting rejection codes.\n\n        First detail writes four header lines. Before each detail the current\n        line counter is tested modulo 20; if zero, page totals and a separator are\n        written, then four headers. Header, subtotal and separator lines count;\n        this is not a fixed twenty-detail page size. Each detail adds amount to\n        page and account accumulators. A page total adds its value to grand total\n        and resets page total. Account totals reset only the account accumulator.\n\n        The EOF branch, if reached after the date predicate, adds TRAN-AMT again\n        to page and account totals, writes page totals and grand totals, but does\n        not write the final account subtotal. It does not print another detail.\n        Thus totals must not be replaced by a mathematically corrected aggregation.\n        If the retained timestamp fails the date predicate at EOF, NEXT SENTENCE\n        skips this finalization entirely.\n\n        Output is the 133-character record stream defined by CVTRA07Y. Detail\n        includes transaction ID, mapped account ID, type code and first 15\n        description characters, category code and first 29 description characters,\n        source and edited amount. Titles are DALYREPT and Daily Transaction Report;\n        totals are labelled Page Total, Account Total and Grand Total.\n        No account, cross-reference or transaction master is modified.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Successful included-record lookups require card, type and category reference records.\n        - Contiguous card ordering is needed for intended group subtotals but is not validated or enforced.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          The failed EOF READ's effect on TRAN-RECORD is runtime-dependent.\n          If the last record is retained and in range, its amount is counted twice\n          in the final page/grand totals. Empty transaction input can encounter\n          uninitialized working-storage values in the predicate/finalization.\n        - |\n          TRANREPT JCL separately unloads, filters using hard-coded dates and sorts\n          card bytes as ZD. Its dates need not match DATEPARM and PIC X card fields\n          can be nonnumeric. Those utility steps are not part of this operation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords, crossReferenceFile, transactionTypeFile, transactionCategoryFile, reportFile]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential DATEPARM file; an empty array and additional ignored records are representable.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                transactionTypeFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                transactionCategoryFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                reportFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal completion; lines reflect the source control flow, including subtotal and EOF quirks.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP mapping for execution failure, not a COBOL business status.\n        Checked nonzero open, write, rewrite or close statuses and unexpected\n        sequential-read statuses normally display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD\n        with ABCODE 999 and TIMING 0. Sequential status 10 is EOF. Explicit lookup\n        exceptions are described per operation. Runtime or binding failures can\n        prevent even reaching that call. Earlier persistent effects and output\n        records may remain; no rollback is implied.\n\n        Posting does not check general status after its cross-reference/account\n        validation reads or account rewrite. Reporting lookup paragraphs handle\n        INVALID KEY only. These gaps are not converted into new guaranteed checks.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  schemas:\n    FileBinding:\n      type: string\n      minLength: 1\n      description: |\n        Opaque deployment-resolved file identifier, a chosen transport convention.\n        May identify an absent, inaccessible or incompatible file; existence is\n        not a schema constraint. Resolution and native file status are reported\n        at execution. OUTPUT resources are opened for output, not append.\n    Amount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,9}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(9)V99 decimal, including zero and negative amounts.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,10}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(10)V99 decimal.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2); not restricted to reference-table membership.\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: |\n        PIC X(26), not an RFC 3339 date-time. Arbitrary text, including blanks\n        and invalid dates, is representable. Generated values use\n        YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 from CURRENT-DATE with no timezone field.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [transactionId, typeCode, categoryCode, source, description, amount, merchantId, merchantName, merchantCity, merchantZip, cardNumber, originalTimestamp, processingTimestamp]\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16) indexed posting key; duplicates are not excluded by the request schema.\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16), not a numeric or Luhn-validated field.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n          default: ''\n          description: Input filler defaults to spaces; posting does not explicitly copy it to TRAN-RECORD.\n    RawTransaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [recordBase64]\n      properties:\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: |\n            Exactly 350 decoded bytes in the native file encoding, including\n            DISPLAY numeric signs and filler. No numeric-content validation is\n            implied. Invalid numeric bytes may cause runtime-dependent failures.\n    TransactionInput:\n      oneOf:\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Layout of persistent ACCTFILE records, CVACT01Y, 300 bytes; indexed by\n        accountId. Provided to document the bound dependency, not to expose a\n        separate account-management operation.\n      required: [accountId, activeStatus, currentBalance, creditLimit, cashCreditLimit, openDate, expirationDate, reissueDate, cycleCredit, cycleDebit, addressZip, groupId]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: Source field ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE; character comparison only.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50 bytes, primary card key; interest also declares an alternate account key.\n      required: [cardNumber, customerId, accountId]\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50 bytes, composite key accountId/typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode, balance]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroup:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50 bytes, composite key groupId/typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode, annualRate]\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        annualRate:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,4}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n          description: S9(4)V99; zero and negative rates are representable.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60 bytes, keyed by typeCode.\n      required: [typeCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60 bytes, keyed by typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [typeCode, categoryCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\n    Reject:\n      type: object\n      required: [originalRecord, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        originalRecord:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n          description: Unpadded text; the native trailer pads this to 76 characters.\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: Complete native 430-byte rejection record, when captured.\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      description: Ordered captured DISPLAY messages, including start/end, errors and file-status diagnostics where reached.\n      items:\n        type: string\n    PostingResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [transactionsProcessed, transactionsRejected, writtenTransactions, rejects, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        transactionsProcessed:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n          description: All successfully read daily records, including rejected records.\n        transactionsRejected:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: Set to 4 when rejects exist; the source does not explicitly set a zero success code.\n        writtenTransactions:\n          type: array\n          description: Records successfully written to TRANFILE; raw form preserves native filler.\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n        rejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Reject'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    InterestResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [generatedTransactions, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        generatedTransactions:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    ReportResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [lines, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        lines:\n          type: array\n          description: Ordered TRANREPT records, with trailing spaces preserved and no added newline characters.\n          items:\n            type: string\n            minLength: 133\n            maxLength: 133\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      required: [message, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        message:\n          type: string\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        stage:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed open, read, lookup, write, rewrite, close or runtime stage, when known.\n        fileBinding:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed native status or displayed four-digit diagnostic; may differ from the true failing status.\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present only when the source abend request is observed.\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        partialPosting:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        partialInterest:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/InterestResult'\n        partialReport:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportResult'\n      description: |\n        Partial artifacts are included only if recoverable and do not imply a\n        complete inventory of persistent effects. Posting reject-file CLOSE\n        diagnostics incorrectly use XREFFILE status in the source.\nx-file-layouts:\n  ACCTFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n    recordLength: 300\n    key: [accountId]\n  XREFFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReference'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n    interestAlternateKey: [accountId]\n  CARDXREF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReference'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n  TCATBALF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n  DISCGRP:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureGroup'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n  TRANTYPE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionType'\n    recordLength: 60\n    key: [typeCode]\n  TRANCATG:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategory'\n    recordLength: 60\n    key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n  TRANFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    recordLength: 350\n    description: Indexed OUTPUT for posting; sequential INPUT for reporting, not automatically the same physical representation.\n  TRANSACT:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    recordLength: 350\n    description: Sequential interest output. COMBTRAN's separate sort and REPRO are outside this boundary.\n"}

event: response.content_part.done
data: {"type":"response.content_part.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_069b54ac0ff5886e016aa3e44a7e4c87d293eccdb221d4f59c","output_index":1,"part":{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Transaction Batch Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for individual invocations of CBTRN02C, CBACT04C and CBTRN03C.\n    HTTP paths, JSON envelopes, file bindings and response status mappings are\n    transport conventions, not interfaces implemented by the COBOL sources.\n    An invocation executes one program, not its enclosing JCL schedule.\n    Referenced indexed files must be provisioned by the execution environment.\n    No file-management, backup, merge, fee-processing or scheduling API is implied.\n\n    Input arrays represent sequential files in the supplied order. Indexed-file\n    bindings identify persistent resources; they are not snapshots supplied by\n    the caller. Output arrays expose records written by the program. No\n    transaction-wide atomicity, rollback, retry or idempotency is promised.\n    Earlier writes and OUTPUT opens can have effects even when a run fails.\n\n    Structured records express valid COBOL field representations, not business\n    validation. Character fields are right-padded with spaces to their PIC width.\n    Numeric identifiers retain leading zeros. Decimal strings are converted to\n    signed fixed-point DISPLAY fields. Raw records permit malformed numeric\n    bytes, arbitrary filler and other file-level failure inputs without imposing\n    invented business checks.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    The corpus supplies no HTTP runtime, file resolver, compiler configuration,\n    encoding configuration or implementation of CEE3ABD. Actual execution\n    availability is an environmental precondition, not established by this contract.\n  - |\n    Native DISPLAY sign encoding, character collation and overflow behavior depend\n    on the COBOL runtime. Arithmetic has no ON SIZE ERROR handling. Raw records\n    require the deployment's native record encoding.\n  - |\n    JCL references SORT, IDCAMS, GDGs and REPROC. REPROC in turn references an\n    unsupplied REPROCT control member. None of these utilities or schedules is\n    assumed to execute through these operations.\n  - |\n    TRANFILE is opened OUTPUT by posting, although the JCL describes a transaction\n    master. Existing master contents are not guaranteed to survive or be available\n    for duplicate detection. This contract does not silently change the open to I-O.\npaths:\n  /posting-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Post one sequential daily transaction file\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN02C. Opens DALYTRAN INPUT, TRANFILE OUTPUT,\n        XREFFILE INPUT, DALYREJS OUTPUT, ACCTFILE I-O and TCATBALF I-O,\n        in that order. Empty input is representable.\n\n        Each successfully read record increments the processed counter. Validation\n        first reads the card cross-reference, then the referenced account.\n        Invalid card produces 0100; missing account produces 0101.\n        On an account read, temporary balance is cycleCredit - cycleDebit + amount\n        in S9(9)V99, not currentBalance + amount. A credit limit smaller than this\n        value sets 0102. ExpirationDate less than the first ten characters of\n        originalTimestamp sets 0103 and overrides 0102. Date comparison is\n        alphanumeric, with no calendar validation. Equality passes both checks.\n        Active status, cash limit, merchant, transaction type/category membership,\n        amount positivity and timestamp syntax are not validated.\n\n        Rejections write the original 350-byte record followed by four reason\n        digits and a space-padded 76-character description. Processing continues.\n        Any rejected records cause RETURN-CODE to be set to 4 at normal completion.\n\n        For a valid record, business fields are copied to the output transaction;\n        processingTimestamp is replaced with the current runtime timestamp.\n        Effects occur in this order: create or add amount to the category balance\n        keyed by account/type/category; add amount to account current balance and,\n        for amount >= 0, cycle credit, otherwise add the signed negative amount to\n        cycle debit; write the indexed transaction keyed by transaction ID.\n        A missing category balance with status 23 is created from an initialized\n        record. No duplicate-ID precheck is performed. A duplicate write may fail\n        after balances have changed.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, but the caller\n        neither rechecks that reason nor writes a reject; it still attempts the\n        transaction write. This is not an ordinary 0109 rejection response.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - The bound files support the stated indexed keys and open modes.\n        - Successful posting requires a card mapping and its account; missing mappings remain legal request cases.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions, transactionFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, categoryBalanceFile, rejectFile]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                transactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                rejectFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal program completion, including per-record business rejections.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Calculate category interest and write system transactions\n      description: |\n        Executes CBACT04C. Opens TCATBALF INPUT for sequential indexed-key\n        traversal, XREFFILE INPUT with alternate account key, DISCGRP INPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O and TRANSACT OUTPUT. It does not post or merge its output\n        into the indexed transaction master and does not update category balances.\n\n        For each account encountered, reads the account and the cross-reference\n        by account ID. A nonzero read status is fatal, including a missing record.\n        Rates are looked up by account group, balance transaction type and category.\n        Status 23 triggers a second lookup using the space-padded group DEFAULT\n        and the same type/category. Failure of that fallback is fatal. Other\n        nonzero primary lookup statuses are fatal.\n\n        Each nonzero rate produces one transaction, even for zero or negative\n        category balances or a computed zero amount. Monthly interest equals\n        categoryBalance * annualRate / 1200, assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED,\n        discarding excess fractional digits. Interest is accumulated per account.\n        Zero rates produce no transaction. The fees paragraph does nothing.\n\n        Transaction ID is the ten-character parameter concatenated with a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001, incremented only on generated transactions.\n        The parameter length is not checked and the parameter is not parsed as a\n        date. The JCL example is 2022071800. Generated type is 01, category is\n        numeric 0005, source is System, description begins \"Int. for a/c \" followed\n        by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is monthly interest, merchant ID\n        is zero and merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces. Card number comes from the\n        account-key cross-reference. Original and processing timestamps are both\n        the current runtime timestamp.\n\n        On transition to a different account, the previous account is rewritten:\n        total accumulated interest is added to current balance and both cycle\n        credit and cycle debit are zeroed, including when all its rates were zero.\n        The source's final-account update branch is unreachable in the normal\n        EOF path: EOF is set inside the N branch and the loop then terminates.\n        Consequently the final account is not rewritten at normal EOF, although\n        its generated transactions have already been written. Empty category\n        input generates no transactions and rewrites no accounts.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - TCATBALF supports sequential traversal by account/type/category key.\n        - XREFFILE must support reading its alternate eleven-digit account key.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          INTCALC JCL also binds XREFFIL1 to an alternate-index path, but the\n          program SELECT uses XREFFILE. Availability and selection of that\n          alternate index are not established by the supplied slice.\n        - |\n          More than 999999 generated records exceeds the six-digit suffix\n          capacity; no explicit overflow or collision handling exists.\n        - |\n          TRAN-RECORD is not initialized before generation. Unassigned filler\n          and description suffix bytes depend on working-storage initialization.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [parameterDate, categoryBalanceFile, crossReferenceFile, disclosureGroupFile, accountFile, outputTransactionFile]\n              properties:\n                parameterDate:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: Exact PIC X(10) transaction-ID prefix; arbitrary text is allowed.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n                parameterLength:\n                  type: integer\n                  minimum: -32768\n                  maximum: 32767\n                  description: Linkage S9(4) COMP length. Not inspected by the program; transport supplies 10 when omitted.\n                  default: 10\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                disclosureGroupFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                outputTransactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal completion; generated output is separate from the transaction master.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/InterestResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-report-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN03C against the supplied sequential transaction records.\n        Opens TRANFILE INPUT, TRANREPT OUTPUT, CARDXREF INPUT, TRANTYPE INPUT,\n        TRANCATG INPUT and DATEPARM INPUT. Reads only the first date parameter\n        record: positions 1-10 are start date, position 11 is ignored and positions\n        12-21 are end date; remaining bytes are ignored. Empty DATEPARM sets EOF\n        and produces an empty report. No calendar or start-before-end check exists.\n\n        For each transaction, the first ten characters of processingTimestamp are\n        compared inclusively to the parameter dates. An out-of-range record uses\n        NEXT SENTENCE to skip the remaining loop body. No sorting occurs in this\n        program. Input order is retained; account subtotals actually delimit\n        contiguous card-number groups, not distinct account IDs. Noncontiguous\n        repeats and multiple cards for an account are not consolidated.\n\n        On a card change, the previous group subtotal is written if reporting has\n        started, then card cross-reference is read. Type and composite type/category\n        descriptions are read for every included record. INVALID KEY in any lookup\n        displays the offending key and invokes the abend routine with status 23.\n        These are fatal failures, not skipped records or posting rejection codes.\n\n        First detail writes four header lines. Before each detail the current\n        line counter is tested modulo 20; if zero, page totals and a separator are\n        written, then four headers. Header, subtotal and separator lines count;\n        this is not a fixed twenty-detail page size. Each detail adds amount to\n        page and account accumulators. A page total adds its value to grand total\n        and resets page total. Account totals reset only the account accumulator.\n\n        The EOF branch, if reached after the date predicate, adds TRAN-AMT again\n        to page and account totals, writes page totals and grand totals, but does\n        not write the final account subtotal. It does not print another detail.\n        Thus totals must not be replaced by a mathematically corrected aggregation.\n        If the retained timestamp fails the date predicate at EOF, NEXT SENTENCE\n        skips this finalization entirely.\n\n        Output is the 133-character record stream defined by CVTRA07Y. Detail\n        includes transaction ID, mapped account ID, type code and first 15\n        description characters, category code and first 29 description characters,\n        source and edited amount. Titles are DALYREPT and Daily Transaction Report;\n        totals are labelled Page Total, Account Total and Grand Total.\n        No account, cross-reference or transaction master is modified.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Successful included-record lookups require card, type and category reference records.\n        - Contiguous card ordering is needed for intended group subtotals but is not validated or enforced.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          The failed EOF READ's effect on TRAN-RECORD is runtime-dependent.\n          If the last record is retained and in range, its amount is counted twice\n          in the final page/grand totals. Empty transaction input can encounter\n          uninitialized working-storage values in the predicate/finalization.\n        - |\n          TRANREPT JCL separately unloads, filters using hard-coded dates and sorts\n          card bytes as ZD. Its dates need not match DATEPARM and PIC X card fields\n          can be nonnumeric. Those utility steps are not part of this operation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords, crossReferenceFile, transactionTypeFile, transactionCategoryFile, reportFile]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential DATEPARM file; an empty array and additional ignored records are representable.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                transactionTypeFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                transactionCategoryFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                reportFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal completion; lines reflect the source control flow, including subtotal and EOF quirks.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP mapping for execution failure, not a COBOL business status.\n        Checked nonzero open, write, rewrite or close statuses and unexpected\n        sequential-read statuses normally display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD\n        with ABCODE 999 and TIMING 0. Sequential status 10 is EOF. Explicit lookup\n        exceptions are described per operation. Runtime or binding failures can\n        prevent even reaching that call. Earlier persistent effects and output\n        records may remain; no rollback is implied.\n\n        Posting does not check general status after its cross-reference/account\n        validation reads or account rewrite. Reporting lookup paragraphs handle\n        INVALID KEY only. These gaps are not converted into new guaranteed checks.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  schemas:\n    FileBinding:\n      type: string\n      minLength: 1\n      description: |\n        Opaque deployment-resolved file identifier, a chosen transport convention.\n        May identify an absent, inaccessible or incompatible file; existence is\n        not a schema constraint. Resolution and native file status are reported\n        at execution. OUTPUT resources are opened for output, not append.\n    Amount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,9}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(9)V99 decimal, including zero and negative amounts.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,10}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(10)V99 decimal.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2); not restricted to reference-table membership.\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: |\n        PIC X(26), not an RFC 3339 date-time. Arbitrary text, including blanks\n        and invalid dates, is representable. Generated values use\n        YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 from CURRENT-DATE with no timezone field.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [transactionId, typeCode, categoryCode, source, description, amount, merchantId, merchantName, merchantCity, merchantZip, cardNumber, originalTimestamp, processingTimestamp]\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16) indexed posting key; duplicates are not excluded by the request schema.\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16), not a numeric or Luhn-validated field.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n          default: ''\n          description: Input filler defaults to spaces; posting does not explicitly copy it to TRAN-RECORD.\n    RawTransaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [recordBase64]\n      properties:\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: |\n            Exactly 350 decoded bytes in the native file encoding, including\n            DISPLAY numeric signs and filler. No numeric-content validation is\n            implied. Invalid numeric bytes may cause runtime-dependent failures.\n    TransactionInput:\n      oneOf:\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Layout of persistent ACCTFILE records, CVACT01Y, 300 bytes; indexed by\n        accountId. Provided to document the bound dependency, not to expose a\n        separate account-management operation.\n      required: [accountId, activeStatus, currentBalance, creditLimit, cashCreditLimit, openDate, expirationDate, reissueDate, cycleCredit, cycleDebit, addressZip, groupId]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: Source field ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE; character comparison only.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50 bytes, primary card key; interest also declares an alternate account key.\n      required: [cardNumber, customerId, accountId]\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50 bytes, composite key accountId/typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode, balance]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroup:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50 bytes, composite key groupId/typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode, annualRate]\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        annualRate:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,4}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n          description: S9(4)V99; zero and negative rates are representable.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60 bytes, keyed by typeCode.\n      required: [typeCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60 bytes, keyed by typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [typeCode, categoryCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\n    Reject:\n      type: object\n      required: [originalRecord, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        originalRecord:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n          description: Unpadded text; the native trailer pads this to 76 characters.\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: Complete native 430-byte rejection record, when captured.\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      description: Ordered captured DISPLAY messages, including start/end, errors and file-status diagnostics where reached.\n      items:\n        type: string\n    PostingResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [transactionsProcessed, transactionsRejected, writtenTransactions, rejects, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        transactionsProcessed:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n          description: All successfully read daily records, including rejected records.\n        transactionsRejected:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: Set to 4 when rejects exist; the source does not explicitly set a zero success code.\n        writtenTransactions:\n          type: array\n          description: Records successfully written to TRANFILE; raw form preserves native filler.\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n        rejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Reject'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    InterestResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [generatedTransactions, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        generatedTransactions:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    ReportResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [lines, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        lines:\n          type: array\n          description: Ordered TRANREPT records, with trailing spaces preserved and no added newline characters.\n          items:\n            type: string\n            minLength: 133\n            maxLength: 133\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      required: [message, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        message:\n          type: string\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        stage:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed open, read, lookup, write, rewrite, close or runtime stage, when known.\n        fileBinding:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed native status or displayed four-digit diagnostic; may differ from the true failing status.\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present only when the source abend request is observed.\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        partialPosting:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        partialInterest:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/InterestResult'\n        partialReport:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportResult'\n      description: |\n        Partial artifacts are included only if recoverable and do not imply a\n        complete inventory of persistent effects. Posting reject-file CLOSE\n        diagnostics incorrectly use XREFFILE status in the source.\nx-file-layouts:\n  ACCTFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n    recordLength: 300\n    key: [accountId]\n  XREFFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReference'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n    interestAlternateKey: [accountId]\n  CARDXREF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReference'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n  TCATBALF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n  DISCGRP:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureGroup'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n  TRANTYPE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionType'\n    recordLength: 60\n    key: [typeCode]\n  TRANCATG:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategory'\n    recordLength: 60\n    key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n  TRANFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    recordLength: 350\n    description: Indexed OUTPUT for posting; sequential INPUT for reporting, not automatically the same physical representation.\n  TRANSACT:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    recordLength: 350\n    description: Sequential interest output. COMBTRAN's separate sort and REPRO are outside this boundary.\n"},"sequence_number":6308}

event: response.output_item.done
data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"id":"msg_069b54ac0ff5886e016aa3e44a7e4c87d293eccdb221d4f59c","type":"message","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"output_text","annotations":[],"logprobs":[],"text":"openapi: 3.1.0\ninfo:\n  title: CardDemo Transaction Batch Boundary\n  version: 1.0.0\n  description: |\n    Contract for individual invocations of CBTRN02C, CBACT04C and CBTRN03C.\n    HTTP paths, JSON envelopes, file bindings and response status mappings are\n    transport conventions, not interfaces implemented by the COBOL sources.\n    An invocation executes one program, not its enclosing JCL schedule.\n    Referenced indexed files must be provisioned by the execution environment.\n    No file-management, backup, merge, fee-processing or scheduling API is implied.\n\n    Input arrays represent sequential files in the supplied order. Indexed-file\n    bindings identify persistent resources; they are not snapshots supplied by\n    the caller. Output arrays expose records written by the program. No\n    transaction-wide atomicity, rollback, retry or idempotency is promised.\n    Earlier writes and OUTPUT opens can have effects even when a run fails.\n\n    Structured records express valid COBOL field representations, not business\n    validation. Character fields are right-padded with spaces to their PIC width.\n    Numeric identifiers retain leading zeros. Decimal strings are converted to\n    signed fixed-point DISPLAY fields. Raw records permit malformed numeric\n    bytes, arbitrary filler and other file-level failure inputs without imposing\n    invented business checks.\nx-uncertainties:\n  - |\n    The corpus supplies no HTTP runtime, file resolver, compiler configuration,\n    encoding configuration or implementation of CEE3ABD. Actual execution\n    availability is an environmental precondition, not established by this contract.\n  - |\n    Native DISPLAY sign encoding, character collation and overflow behavior depend\n    on the COBOL runtime. Arithmetic has no ON SIZE ERROR handling. Raw records\n    require the deployment's native record encoding.\n  - |\n    JCL references SORT, IDCAMS, GDGs and REPROC. REPROC in turn references an\n    unsupplied REPROCT control member. None of these utilities or schedules is\n    assumed to execute through these operations.\n  - |\n    TRANFILE is opened OUTPUT by posting, although the JCL describes a transaction\n    master. Existing master contents are not guaranteed to survive or be available\n    for duplicate detection. This contract does not silently change the open to I-O.\npaths:\n  /posting-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: postDailyTransactions\n      summary: Post one sequential daily transaction file\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN02C. Opens DALYTRAN INPUT, TRANFILE OUTPUT,\n        XREFFILE INPUT, DALYREJS OUTPUT, ACCTFILE I-O and TCATBALF I-O,\n        in that order. Empty input is representable.\n\n        Each successfully read record increments the processed counter. Validation\n        first reads the card cross-reference, then the referenced account.\n        Invalid card produces 0100; missing account produces 0101.\n        On an account read, temporary balance is cycleCredit - cycleDebit + amount\n        in S9(9)V99, not currentBalance + amount. A credit limit smaller than this\n        value sets 0102. ExpirationDate less than the first ten characters of\n        originalTimestamp sets 0103 and overrides 0102. Date comparison is\n        alphanumeric, with no calendar validation. Equality passes both checks.\n        Active status, cash limit, merchant, transaction type/category membership,\n        amount positivity and timestamp syntax are not validated.\n\n        Rejections write the original 350-byte record followed by four reason\n        digits and a space-padded 76-character description. Processing continues.\n        Any rejected records cause RETURN-CODE to be set to 4 at normal completion.\n\n        For a valid record, business fields are copied to the output transaction;\n        processingTimestamp is replaced with the current runtime timestamp.\n        Effects occur in this order: create or add amount to the category balance\n        keyed by account/type/category; add amount to account current balance and,\n        for amount >= 0, cycle credit, otherwise add the signed negative amount to\n        cycle debit; write the indexed transaction keyed by transaction ID.\n        A missing category balance with status 23 is created from an initialized\n        record. No duplicate-ID precheck is performed. A duplicate write may fail\n        after balances have changed.\n\n        Account REWRITE INVALID KEY sets internal reason 0109, but the caller\n        neither rechecks that reason nor writes a reject; it still attempts the\n        transaction write. This is not an ordinary 0109 rejection response.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - The bound files support the stated indexed keys and open modes.\n        - Successful posting requires a card mapping and its account; missing mappings remain legal request cases.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [dailyTransactions, transactionFile, crossReferenceFile, accountFile, categoryBalanceFile, rejectFile]\n              properties:\n                dailyTransactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                transactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                rejectFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal program completion, including per-record business rejections.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /interest-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateInterestTransactions\n      summary: Calculate category interest and write system transactions\n      description: |\n        Executes CBACT04C. Opens TCATBALF INPUT for sequential indexed-key\n        traversal, XREFFILE INPUT with alternate account key, DISCGRP INPUT,\n        ACCTFILE I-O and TRANSACT OUTPUT. It does not post or merge its output\n        into the indexed transaction master and does not update category balances.\n\n        For each account encountered, reads the account and the cross-reference\n        by account ID. A nonzero read status is fatal, including a missing record.\n        Rates are looked up by account group, balance transaction type and category.\n        Status 23 triggers a second lookup using the space-padded group DEFAULT\n        and the same type/category. Failure of that fallback is fatal. Other\n        nonzero primary lookup statuses are fatal.\n\n        Each nonzero rate produces one transaction, even for zero or negative\n        category balances or a computed zero amount. Monthly interest equals\n        categoryBalance * annualRate / 1200, assigned to S9(9)V99 without ROUNDED,\n        discarding excess fractional digits. Interest is accumulated per account.\n        Zero rates produce no transaction. The fees paragraph does nothing.\n\n        Transaction ID is the ten-character parameter concatenated with a six-digit\n        counter starting at 000001, incremented only on generated transactions.\n        The parameter length is not checked and the parameter is not parsed as a\n        date. The JCL example is 2022071800. Generated type is 01, category is\n        numeric 0005, source is System, description begins \"Int. for a/c \" followed\n        by the eleven-digit account ID, amount is monthly interest, merchant ID\n        is zero and merchant name/city/ZIP are spaces. Card number comes from the\n        account-key cross-reference. Original and processing timestamps are both\n        the current runtime timestamp.\n\n        On transition to a different account, the previous account is rewritten:\n        total accumulated interest is added to current balance and both cycle\n        credit and cycle debit are zeroed, including when all its rates were zero.\n        The source's final-account update branch is unreachable in the normal\n        EOF path: EOF is set inside the N branch and the loop then terminates.\n        Consequently the final account is not rewritten at normal EOF, although\n        its generated transactions have already been written. Empty category\n        input generates no transactions and rewrites no accounts.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - TCATBALF supports sequential traversal by account/type/category key.\n        - XREFFILE must support reading its alternate eleven-digit account key.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          INTCALC JCL also binds XREFFIL1 to an alternate-index path, but the\n          program SELECT uses XREFFILE. Availability and selection of that\n          alternate index are not established by the supplied slice.\n        - |\n          More than 999999 generated records exceeds the six-digit suffix\n          capacity; no explicit overflow or collision handling exists.\n        - |\n          TRAN-RECORD is not initialized before generation. Unassigned filler\n          and description suffix bytes depend on working-storage initialization.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [parameterDate, categoryBalanceFile, crossReferenceFile, disclosureGroupFile, accountFile, outputTransactionFile]\n              properties:\n                parameterDate:\n                  type: string\n                  minLength: 10\n                  maxLength: 10\n                  description: Exact PIC X(10) transaction-ID prefix; arbitrary text is allowed.\n                  examples: ['2022071800']\n                parameterLength:\n                  type: integer\n                  minimum: -32768\n                  maximum: 32767\n                  description: Linkage S9(4) COMP length. Not inspected by the program; transport supplies 10 when omitted.\n                  default: 10\n                categoryBalanceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                disclosureGroupFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                accountFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                outputTransactionFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal completion; generated output is separate from the transaction master.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/InterestResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\n  /transaction-report-runs:\n    post:\n      operationId: generateTransactionReport\n      summary: Produce the fixed-width transaction detail report\n      description: |\n        Executes CBTRN03C against the supplied sequential transaction records.\n        Opens TRANFILE INPUT, TRANREPT OUTPUT, CARDXREF INPUT, TRANTYPE INPUT,\n        TRANCATG INPUT and DATEPARM INPUT. Reads only the first date parameter\n        record: positions 1-10 are start date, position 11 is ignored and positions\n        12-21 are end date; remaining bytes are ignored. Empty DATEPARM sets EOF\n        and produces an empty report. No calendar or start-before-end check exists.\n\n        For each transaction, the first ten characters of processingTimestamp are\n        compared inclusively to the parameter dates. An out-of-range record uses\n        NEXT SENTENCE to skip the remaining loop body. No sorting occurs in this\n        program. Input order is retained; account subtotals actually delimit\n        contiguous card-number groups, not distinct account IDs. Noncontiguous\n        repeats and multiple cards for an account are not consolidated.\n\n        On a card change, the previous group subtotal is written if reporting has\n        started, then card cross-reference is read. Type and composite type/category\n        descriptions are read for every included record. INVALID KEY in any lookup\n        displays the offending key and invokes the abend routine with status 23.\n        These are fatal failures, not skipped records or posting rejection codes.\n\n        First detail writes four header lines. Before each detail the current\n        line counter is tested modulo 20; if zero, page totals and a separator are\n        written, then four headers. Header, subtotal and separator lines count;\n        this is not a fixed twenty-detail page size. Each detail adds amount to\n        page and account accumulators. A page total adds its value to grand total\n        and resets page total. Account totals reset only the account accumulator.\n\n        The EOF branch, if reached after the date predicate, adds TRAN-AMT again\n        to page and account totals, writes page totals and grand totals, but does\n        not write the final account subtotal. It does not print another detail.\n        Thus totals must not be replaced by a mathematically corrected aggregation.\n        If the retained timestamp fails the date predicate at EOF, NEXT SENTENCE\n        skips this finalization entirely.\n\n        Output is the 133-character record stream defined by CVTRA07Y. Detail\n        includes transaction ID, mapped account ID, type code and first 15\n        description characters, category code and first 29 description characters,\n        source and edited amount. Titles are DALYREPT and Daily Transaction Report;\n        totals are labelled Page Total, Account Total and Grand Total.\n        No account, cross-reference or transaction master is modified.\n      x-preconditions:\n        - Successful included-record lookups require card, type and category reference records.\n        - Contiguous card ordering is needed for intended group subtotals but is not validated or enforced.\n      x-uncertainties:\n        - |\n          The failed EOF READ's effect on TRAN-RECORD is runtime-dependent.\n          If the last record is retained and in range, its amount is counted twice\n          in the final page/grand totals. Empty transaction input can encounter\n          uninitialized working-storage values in the predicate/finalization.\n        - |\n          TRANREPT JCL separately unloads, filters using hard-coded dates and sorts\n          card bytes as ZD. Its dates need not match DATEPARM and PIC X card fields\n          can be nonnumeric. Those utility steps are not part of this operation.\n      requestBody:\n        required: true\n        content:\n          application/json:\n            schema:\n              type: object\n              additionalProperties: false\n              required: [transactions, dateParameterRecords, crossReferenceFile, transactionTypeFile, transactionCategoryFile, reportFile]\n              properties:\n                transactions:\n                  type: array\n                  items:\n                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n                dateParameterRecords:\n                  type: array\n                  description: Sequential DATEPARM file; an empty array and additional ignored records are representable.\n                  items:\n                    type: string\n                    minLength: 80\n                    maxLength: 80\n                crossReferenceFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                transactionTypeFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                transactionCategoryFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n                reportFile:\n                  $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n      responses:\n        '200':\n          description: Normal completion; lines reflect the source control flow, including subtotal and EOF quirks.\n          content:\n            application/json:\n              schema:\n                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportResult'\n        '500':\n          $ref: '#/components/responses/ExecutionFailure'\ncomponents:\n  responses:\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      description: |\n        Chosen HTTP mapping for execution failure, not a COBOL business status.\n        Checked nonzero open, write, rewrite or close statuses and unexpected\n        sequential-read statuses normally display diagnostics and call CEE3ABD\n        with ABCODE 999 and TIMING 0. Sequential status 10 is EOF. Explicit lookup\n        exceptions are described per operation. Runtime or binding failures can\n        prevent even reaching that call. Earlier persistent effects and output\n        records may remain; no rollback is implied.\n\n        Posting does not check general status after its cross-reference/account\n        validation reads or account rewrite. Reporting lookup paragraphs handle\n        INVALID KEY only. These gaps are not converted into new guaranteed checks.\n      content:\n        application/json:\n          schema:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/ExecutionFailure'\n  schemas:\n    FileBinding:\n      type: string\n      minLength: 1\n      description: |\n        Opaque deployment-resolved file identifier, a chosen transport convention.\n        May identify an absent, inaccessible or incompatible file; existence is\n        not a schema constraint. Resolution and native file status are reported\n        at execution. OUTPUT resources are opened for output, not append.\n    Amount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,9}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(9)V99 decimal, including zero and negative amounts.\n    AccountAmount:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,10}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n      description: Signed S9(10)V99 decimal.\n    AccountId:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{11}$'\n    CategoryCode:\n      type: string\n      pattern: '^[0-9]{4}$'\n    TypeCode:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 2\n      description: PIC X(2); not restricted to reference-table membership.\n    Timestamp:\n      type: string\n      maxLength: 26\n      description: |\n        PIC X(26), not an RFC 3339 date-time. Arbitrary text, including blanks\n        and invalid dates, is representable. Generated values use\n        YYYY-MM-DD-HH.MM.SS.hh0000 from CURRENT-DATE with no timezone field.\n    Transaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [transactionId, typeCode, categoryCode, source, description, amount, merchantId, merchantName, merchantCity, merchantZip, cardNumber, originalTimestamp, processingTimestamp]\n      properties:\n        transactionId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16) indexed posting key; duplicates are not excluded by the request schema.\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        source:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 100\n        amount:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        merchantId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        merchantName:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantCity:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        merchantZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n          description: PIC X(16), not a numeric or Luhn-validated field.\n        originalTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        processingTimestamp:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Timestamp'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 20\n          default: ''\n          description: Input filler defaults to spaces; posting does not explicitly copy it to TRAN-RECORD.\n    RawTransaction:\n      type: object\n      additionalProperties: false\n      required: [recordBase64]\n      properties:\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: |\n            Exactly 350 decoded bytes in the native file encoding, including\n            DISPLAY numeric signs and filler. No numeric-content validation is\n            implied. Invalid numeric bytes may cause runtime-dependent failures.\n    TransactionInput:\n      oneOf:\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n        - $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n    Account:\n      type: object\n      description: |\n        Layout of persistent ACCTFILE records, CVACT01Y, 300 bytes; indexed by\n        accountId. Provided to document the bound dependency, not to expose a\n        separate account-management operation.\n      required: [accountId, activeStatus, currentBalance, creditLimit, cashCreditLimit, openDate, expirationDate, reissueDate, cycleCredit, cycleDebit, addressZip, groupId]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        activeStatus:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 1\n        currentBalance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        creditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cashCreditLimit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        openDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        expirationDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n          description: Source field ACCT-EXPIRAION-DATE; character comparison only.\n        reissueDate:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        cycleCredit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        cycleDebit:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountAmount'\n        addressZip:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 178\n    CrossReference:\n      type: object\n      description: CVACT03Y, 50 bytes, primary card key; interest also declares an alternate account key.\n      required: [cardNumber, customerId, accountId]\n      properties:\n        cardNumber:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 16\n        customerId:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^[0-9]{9}$'\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 14\n    CategoryBalance:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA01Y, 50 bytes, composite key accountId/typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode, balance]\n      properties:\n        accountId:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/AccountId'\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        balance:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Amount'\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 22\n    DisclosureGroup:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA02Y, 50 bytes, composite key groupId/typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode, annualRate]\n      properties:\n        groupId:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 10\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        annualRate:\n          type: string\n          pattern: '^-?[0-9]{1,4}\\.[0-9]{2}$'\n          description: S9(4)V99; zero and negative rates are representable.\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 28\n    TransactionType:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA03Y, 60 bytes, keyed by typeCode.\n      required: [typeCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 8\n    TransactionCategory:\n      type: object\n      description: CVTRA04Y, 60 bytes, keyed by typeCode/categoryCode.\n      required: [typeCode, categoryCode, description]\n      properties:\n        typeCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/TypeCode'\n        categoryCode:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryCode'\n        description:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 50\n        filler:\n          type: string\n          maxLength: 4\n    Reject:\n      type: object\n      required: [originalRecord, reasonCode, reasonDescription]\n      properties:\n        originalRecord:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/RawTransaction'\n        reasonCode:\n          type: string\n          enum: ['0100', '0101', '0102', '0103']\n        reasonDescription:\n          type: string\n          enum:\n            - INVALID CARD NUMBER FOUND\n            - ACCOUNT RECORD NOT FOUND\n            - OVERLIMIT TRANSACTION\n            - TRANSACTION RECEIVED AFTER ACCT EXPIRATION\n          description: Unpadded text; the native trailer pads this to 76 characters.\n        recordBase64:\n          type: string\n          contentEncoding: base64\n          description: Complete native 430-byte rejection record, when captured.\n    Diagnostics:\n      type: array\n      description: Ordered captured DISPLAY messages, including start/end, errors and file-status diagnostics where reached.\n      items:\n        type: string\n    PostingResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [transactionsProcessed, transactionsRejected, writtenTransactions, rejects, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        transactionsProcessed:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n          description: All successfully read daily records, including rejected records.\n        transactionsRejected:\n          type: integer\n          minimum: 0\n          maximum: 999999999\n        returnCode:\n          type: integer\n          description: Set to 4 when rejects exist; the source does not explicitly set a zero success code.\n        writtenTransactions:\n          type: array\n          description: Records successfully written to TRANFILE; raw form preserves native filler.\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n        rejects:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/Reject'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    InterestResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [generatedTransactions, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        generatedTransactions:\n          type: array\n          items:\n            $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionInput'\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    ReportResult:\n      type: object\n      required: [lines, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        lines:\n          type: array\n          description: Ordered TRANREPT records, with trailing spaces preserved and no added newline characters.\n          items:\n            type: string\n            minLength: 133\n            maxLength: 133\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n    ExecutionFailure:\n      type: object\n      required: [message, diagnostics]\n      properties:\n        message:\n          type: string\n        program:\n          type: string\n          enum: [CBTRN02C, CBACT04C, CBTRN03C]\n        stage:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed open, read, lookup, write, rewrite, close or runtime stage, when known.\n        fileBinding:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileBinding'\n        fileStatus:\n          type: string\n          description: Observed native status or displayed four-digit diagnostic; may differ from the true failing status.\n        abendCode:\n          type: integer\n          const: 999\n          description: Present only when the source abend request is observed.\n        diagnostics:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/Diagnostics'\n        partialPosting:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/PostingResult'\n        partialInterest:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/InterestResult'\n        partialReport:\n          $ref: '#/components/schemas/ReportResult'\n      description: |\n        Partial artifacts are included only if recoverable and do not imply a\n        complete inventory of persistent effects. Posting reject-file CLOSE\n        diagnostics incorrectly use XREFFILE status in the source.\nx-file-layouts:\n  ACCTFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Account'\n    recordLength: 300\n    key: [accountId]\n  XREFFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReference'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n    interestAlternateKey: [accountId]\n  CARDXREF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CrossReference'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [cardNumber]\n  TCATBALF:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CategoryBalance'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [accountId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n  DISCGRP:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/DisclosureGroup'\n    recordLength: 50\n    key: [groupId, typeCode, categoryCode]\n  TRANTYPE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionType'\n    recordLength: 60\n    key: [typeCode]\n  TRANCATG:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/TransactionCategory'\n    recordLength: 60\n    key: [typeCode, categoryCode]\n  TRANFILE:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    recordLength: 350\n    description: Indexed OUTPUT for posting; sequential INPUT for reporting, not automatically the same physical representation.\n  TRANSACT:\n    schema:\n      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Transaction'\n    recordLength: 350\n    description: Sequential interest output. COMBTRAN's separate sort and REPRO are outside this boundary.\n"}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"},"output_index":1,"sequence_number":6309}

